  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "Householder",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, by reason of scale, siting and design, would be an undesirable addition which would result in a complex roof form and overly bulky rear elevation which would result in harm to the character and appearance of the original dwelling.&nbsp; It would fail to respect or reflect the character and appearance of the original dwelling, the terrace row, and the wider Becontree Estate. The proposal would appear visually intrusive and out-keeping with the local distinctiveness and historic character of the&nbsp;Becontree Estate, therefore causing detrimental harm to the non-designated heritage asset. The proposal would therefore be contrary to the following policies which seek to ensure that developments are sympathetic to local character:National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December, 2024) Policies&nbsp;D4 and HC1 of the London Plan (March 2021) The Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012) Policies SPP6, SP2, DMD1, DMD4&nbsp;and DMD5 of The Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September, 2024)"
  ],
